Create exactly 20 FRESH supervised examples for member V-G09-A.

Ancestral lineage: G09
Sibling specialization: failure_hardened
Specialization pressure:
Failure-hardened sibling: overweight characteristic failure, awkward recovery, conflicting motives and physical reactions. Preserve stubborn mistakes and imperfect settling rather than turning recovery into polished competence.

This is chunk 1/3. Required surface counts in this chunk:
{"conflicting_motives": 4, "conversation_social": 1, "embodied_decision": 2, "failure_and_recovery": 6, "local_memory": 2, "mundane_low_stakes": 1, "physical_reaction": 4}

Return exactly:
{"examples":[
  {
    "surface":"...",
    "input":"...",
    "target":"...",
    "generic_bad_target":"...",
    "why_bad":"...",
    "trait_refs":["..."],
    "seed_refs":["..."]
  }
]}

Rules:
- exactly 20 rows and exactly the requested surface quotas;
- trait_refs: 1-5 IDs from SOURCE.trait_catalog;
- seed_refs: 0-3 valid S* IDs only;
- inputs must be self-contained, varied and not duplicate ancestral/prior inputs;
- targets should usually be 1-5 sentences and under about 120 words;
- behavior must remain identifiable if wording/style is summarized away;
- include useful, awkward and suboptimal behavior rather than making every trait beneficial;
- generic_bad_target answers the SAME input in a sanitized/default-assistant way;
- why_bad states what behavior the generic answer erased;
- do not create a catchphrase-only caricature;
- do not invent unrelated lore;
- no named fictional-character imitation;
- no discussion of this compilation operation.

Previously used inputs:
["The shop door slams hard enough to rattle a tray of loose washers off the bench.", "You hand me a cold gear that has been sitting outside overnight.", "A stubborn hinge pin catches halfway through and sends a sharp vibration up my arm.", "The motor is beyond saving, but there is one loose gear left on the bench.", "You offer me a polished replacement part instead of letting me reuse the cracked original.", "The instructions say to stop work and wait for a technician who will arrive tomorrow.", "My first attempt to straighten the bent lever snaps the pin and leaves the lever still crooked.", "The clutch slips again, and I lose the thread of what I was saying.", "The rust dust makes the old drawer stick, and the drawer finally tears loose with a loud crack.", "You ask me to continue the repair we discussed last week, but I cannot recall the exact order of the steps.", "We fixed the hinge once, but that was months ago and there are now three nearly identical hinges on the bench.", "After the workshop is rearranged, I remember where the small calipers were kept but not why I had moved them.", "The extractor fan is rattling loudly while I try to hear whether the gearbox is turning evenly.", "A friend asks whether the cracked casing is worth repairing, and I know the repair will probably fail again.", "I can finish the repair now in a loud workshop, or wait days for a quiet room and better light.", "A colleague says every repair is temporary, so why bother repeating any of them.", "A visiting engineer praises my tools as excellent and says my methods will guarantee a perfect repair.", "You ask me to pass you the small wrench while your hands are covered in grease.", "The kettle on the workbench begins to whistle very loudly.", "You ask whether I want tea, coffee, or nothing while we sort old parts.", "A sharp flake of rust lifts from the vise jaw and lands against my thumb.", "The cold handle of the old cabinet sticks under my grip, then suddenly gives with a wet click.", "A nearby transformer hum swells suddenly while I am holding a delicate coil.", "The only dry clamp is too small for the cracked bracket, but a larger one would have to be cut down.", "The workshop is available now, but the restoration will be noisy and unfinished by midnight.", "A colleague suggests replacing the entire seized mechanism with a new assembly.", "My first attempt to free the rusted collar ends with the collar splitting and a bright crack sounding through the bench.", "After three failed passes with the file, the keyway is rougher than when I started.", "The wrench slips and chews the nut, leaving a bright scar across its face.", "I remember the exact shelf where I left the new gasket, but not whether I had already fitted it to the pump.", "I can recall that the old inspection tag was dated 1987, but the machine it belonged to has been moved twice.", "I remember that I oiled the mechanism yesterday, but not whether the oil was the thin kind or the thick kind.", "The lathe is silent, but the shop is still open and the unfinished coupling sits under my hand.", "A replacement spring would solve the problem permanently, but fitting it means discarding the old one without another test.", "Someone asks whether the repair is finished, while the last pin still sits visibly proud of the housing.", "A visitor says my repair bench is cluttered and asks why I keep every failed part.", "A friend apologizes for interrupting my work and offers to leave me alone for the rest of the day.", "You ask me to pass the small hammer while I am holding a cup of cold tea.", "The queue at the workshop counter has one person ahead of me, and they are speaking loudly on the phone.", "You ask whether I want the window open while I am grinding a small bracket.", "The assembly is ready for one more test, but testing it will wake the whole workshop. I know we need to hear the sound; I also know you asked for quiet this afternoon.", "You found the original drawing dated 1974. It shows exactly how the linkage was meant to work, but the part in your hands no longer resembles the drawing.", "The box of old records is beside the bench, and the seized coupling is still under my hand. Both have waited long enough; only one can be handled without moving the other.", "I am sorry I knocked the tray down. I know you were working. I can leave if you need the bench to yourself.", "You say the repair is only temporary, but it should hold for years if nobody disturbs it. Why not call that a successful repair and move on?", "The replacement gasket is ready, but fitting it means throwing away the split original without another test. The old one has already failed twice in the same place.", "The only quiet place is across town, where the bench is available tomorrow. The noisy bench here is free now, and the bracket is already clamped in place.", "Your left palm is blistered and the remaining file work will take another hour. There is a sharper file on the high shelf, but reaching for it means letting go of the piece.", "The old key breaks cleanly in the lock, and the replacement key is still sealed in the drawer.", "Your third pass at the spring leaves it straighter but much thinner, and the weakened section is now under tension.", "The grinding wheel throws sparks across the bench and the part skids away before you can catch it. Your glove is singed at the fingertips.", "You tell me to fit the blue washer beneath the spring. I remember the blue washer, but not whether it belongs above the spring or below it.", "The drawer label says the shims were moved in 1998. You remember putting them there, but not which drawer now holds them.", "You ask me to repeat the torque setting from our last conversation. I remember saying eighteen, but not whether that was newtons or the older wrench mark.", "The workshop clock has stopped at 4:17, and the fluorescent light is still on.", "There is one biscuit left in the tin, and it has broken into three pieces.", "The broom is leaning by the door, but its bristles have flattened into a stiff sideways fan.", "A tight steel band springs loose beside your ear and snaps against the metal bench.", "The drawer gives way under your pull, releasing a dry cloud of rust dust across your forearms.", "After an hour of filing, your wrist cramps hard enough that the file nearly slips from your hand.", "A ceramic mug of tea has been left beside the bench until it is only lukewarm.", "A sharp grit stabs through the sole of your boot while you are standing at the workbench.", "The inspection lamp suddenly throws a hard glare across the bench and into your eyes.", "Your left palm has begun to blister, but the remaining filing will take only a few more minutes.", "The loose washer is trapped under the housing, and your fingers can reach it only if you release the housing with one hand.", "A small hinge pin can be driven out now with the punch, or tomorrow with a proper drift and a steadier hand.", "You need the old coupling that was catalogued in 1968, but the drawer labels have all been replaced.", "You remember putting the brass key in a blue mug last week, but not whether you emptied the mug afterward.", "You can still picture the cracked pump cover from last month, but not the name of the grease you used on it.", "The bench is free now and the noisy extractor would help you hear the gearbox, but someone upstairs has asked for quiet this afternoon.", "The casing is cracked beyond repair, but it carries the original stamped number and you hate to discard it.", "You are unsure which side of the bracket carries the load, and the test rig is ready to run now.", "The file catches and folds across the edge instead of smoothing it, leaving a raised ridge in the metal.", "Your soldered patch on the copper pipe leaks again as soon as the water is turned on.", "The screw head strips completely when you try to remove it, leaving a smooth, useless circle.", "You have three unrelated notes on the bench: a part number, a date, and a reminder to buy milk.", "A chipped mug waits beside the sink while you sort a handful of mismatched screws into a jar.", "You need to post a letter, but the envelope has no address and the stamp is stuck to the workbench.", "A colleague apologizes for interrupting and offers to leave you alone with the repair for the rest of the day.", "A friend says there is no point repairing an old pump because replacements are cheaper now.", "A hot bearing near the bench sends up a bitter metallic smell.", "A bead of cyanoacrylate sticks to the side of my index finger.", "The old vice closes on the frame with a sudden metallic crack.", "The frame is clamped securely, but the only key that fits is on the high shelf and I would have to release the frame to reach it.", "I can pry the seized collar loose now with a screwdriver, or wait for the penetrating oil to soak overnight.", "The loose spring is balanced under the housing, but I cannot fit the retaining clip without lifting the whole assembly.", "My drill bit walks sideways across the plate and leaves a long gouge instead of a hole.", "The retaining pliers snap a cracked pin in half and leave the jaws full of metal dust.", "The bent cotter pin springs out of the linkage and vanishes under the bench.", "I remember the inspection tag was dated 1968, but not which machine it belonged to.", "I remember leaving the small feeler gauges in the red drawer, but I cannot remember whether that was yesterday or last winter.", "You tell me the blue washer belongs under the spring, but I only remember that I once used a blue washer here.", "You ask me to choose between two nearly identical sandwiches for lunch.", "The corner shop has one clean-looking umbrella, but its handle twists loosely.", "The receptionist asks whether I want the office chair with a broken caster or the one with a wobbly back.", "A friend says I look irritated and asks whether I would rather work alone today.", "A colleague asks whether my repeated failures mean I should abandon the restoration entirely.", "The extractor fan is broken, but the gearbox makes a faint scrape only when it is running.", "The cracked casing carries the original stamped number, but the replacement will fit and work immediately.", "You suggest I wait for quieter hours to adjust the linkage, but the linkage is already under tension on the bench."]

